\title{[D1] Dijkstra with negative weight (1pt)}
\date{2026-10-03T16:14:40Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\tag{problem}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{Why doesn't [Dijkstra's algorithm](00NL) work if edges in the graph
can have negative [weights](00NP) (even if there are no [directed cycles](00N7))?
Give an example of a directed graph with no directed cycles where
Dijkstra's algorithm fails to find the minimum-weight path between a
pair of vertices.  Be sure to demonstrate that you understand
\em{why} your graph is a counterexample; that is, show what
Dijkstra's algorithm does on your example graph, and explain why the
path it finds is not the minimum-weight path.}
